<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-chirat-mollusc-shell-marginal-buckling-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Chirat, Moulton & Goriely (2013) & Erlich et al. (2016) mollusc shell marginal buckling and antimarginal rib morphogenesis — MorphoEval overall 91.4/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 2 (v2) remediated evaluation of `2013-chirat-mollusc-shell-marginal-buckling.py` (consensus score 91.3/100, up from 53.1/100 in Pass 1). The remediated script implements spectral L-BFGS-B energy minimization of the fourth-order nonlinear Winkler-beam mantle margin (`relax_winkler_mantle_margin`, L198-297), validates the supercritical pitchfork amplitude law (r=0.9999 across P/P_c in [0.65, 1.85]) and subcritical negative control (P/P_c=0.65 -> 0 ribs), synthesizes 3D accretionary shells across 4 morphospace regimes (smooth, isometric *Pecten*, intercalating multicostate *Chlamys*/*Spirifer*, and episodic spiny varix *Murex*), collapses 12 empirical species across 4 clades onto the quarter-power law lambda_c = 2*pi*(EI/k)^(1/4) (r=1.0000, exponent alpha=0.2500), and segments n=14 primary radial costae (dtheta=9.40 deg, CV=0.2196) on the SHA-256-locked *Pecten jacobaeus* specimen, backed by 4 machine-checked Lean 4 theorems. Overall 91.4/100 (faithfulness 91.1, reproducibility 92.0); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit HEAD; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.4.2, scipy 1.17.0, matplotlib 3.10.8, Pillow 12.1.1. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 93, Morphological realism / specimen match 90, Parameter expressivity 89, Morphometric validation 92, Source and data traceability 94, Code-to-model traceability 91, Reproducibility package 91. Output judged: docs/media/mollusc_shell_marginal_buckling_comparison.png: rendered output of 2013-chirat-mollusc-shell-marginal-buckling.py at HEAD, image/png, 1221144 B, 2255×1465 px, artifact_sha256 a8119b0f6dffce4653c783e3b8449feebcf9dc64fd08b88f2ee277753a8426fe (sha256 a8119b0f6dffce4653c783e3b8449feebcf9dc64fd08b88f2ee277753a8426fe), spec_fingerprint 890d42a5978673be401f72aa812cb4358400a79d2ca684773dc085cd5735c833. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 890d42a5978673be401f72aa812cb4358400a79d2ca684773dc085cd5735c833; artifact_sha256: a8119b0f6dffce4653c783e3b8449feebcf9dc64fd08b88f2ee277753a8426fe; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/mollusc_shell_marginal_buckling/mollusc_shell_marginal_buckling_reference.json=dec7d148f176932a..., datasets/mollusc_shell_marginal_buckling/ribbed_bivalve_shell_specimen.jpg=a0ac69e8a9be3928..., datasets/mollusc_shell_marginal_buckling/scout_manifest.json=2fb38cc60b112598...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-19-mollusc-shell-marginal-buckling-audit." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Couple the 1D marginal Winkler-beam solver to a full 3D finite-strain morphoelastic shell finite-element mesh (Rudraraju et al. 2019 PLoS Comput. Biol.) to resolve self-contact closure of hollow tubular Murex spines.",
        "remediation needed: Incorporate predator-induced marginal shell damage and localized mantle repair perturbations into the accretionary growth trajectory." ;
    pk:hasScore 9.14e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-chirat-mollusc-shell-marginal-buckling-parameter-expressivity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
